{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates Java code to Python 3 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following Java 8 code to Python 3 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original Java 8 code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\nimport java.io.*;\nimport java.util.*;\n\npublic class Variant5 {\n    static class Input {\n        private final InputStream in;\n        private final byte[] buf = new byte[1 << 16];\n        private int ptr, len;\n\n        public Input(InputStream stream) {\n            in = stream;\n        }\n\n        private int read() throws IOException {\n            if (ptr >= len) {\n                len = in.read(buf);\n                ptr = 0;\n                if (len <= 0) return -1;\n            }\n            return buf[ptr++];\n        }\n\n        public int nextInt() throws IOException {\n            int c = read();\n            while (c <= 32) c = read();\n            int sign = 1;\n            if (c == '-') {\n                sign = -1;\n                c = read();\n            }\n            int val = 0;\n            while (c > 32) {\n                val = val * 10 + c - '0';\n                c = read();\n            }\n            return val * sign;\n        }\n\n        public int[] nextIntArray(int n) throws IOException {\n            int[] arr = new int[n];\n            for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) arr[i] = nextInt();\n            return arr;\n        }\n    }\n\n    public static void main(String[] args) throws Exception {\n        Input in = new Input(System.in);\n        int n = in.nextInt();\n        int b = in.nextInt();\n        int[] a = in.nextIntArray(n);\n\n        int[] odd = new int[n + 1];\n        int[] even = new int[n + 1];\n\n        for (int i = 1; i <= n; i++) {\n            odd[i] = odd[i - 1] + (a[i - 1] & 1);\n            even[i] = even[i - 1] + ((a[i - 1] ^ 1) & 1);\n        }\n\n        int last = 0;\n        PriorityQueue<Integer> costs = new PriorityQueue<>();\n        for (int i = 1; i < n; i++) {\n            int o = odd[i] - odd[last];\n            int e = even[i] - even[last];\n            if (o == e) {\n                costs.add(Math.abs(a[i] - a[i - 1]));\n                last = i;\n            }\n        }\n\n        int total = 0;\n        int count = 0;\n        while (!costs.isEmpty() && total <= b) {\n            total += costs.poll();\n            count++;\n        }\n\n        if (count == 0) {\n            System.out.println(0);\n        } else {\n            System.out.println(costs.isEmpty() && total <= b ? count : count - 1);\n        }\n    }\n}\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "qwen/qwen3-coder-next"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\nimport sys\nimport heapq\n\nclass Input:\n    def __init__(self, stream):\n        self.in_stream = stream\n        self.buf = bytearray(1 << 16)\n        self.ptr = 0\n        self.len = 0\n\n    def read(self):\n        if self.ptr >= self.len:\n            self.len = self.in_stream.readinto(self.buf)\n            self.ptr = 0\n            if self.len <= 0:\n                return -1\n        c = self.buf[self.ptr]\n        self.ptr += 1\n        return c\n\n    def nextInt(self):\n        c = self.read()\n        while c <= 32:\n            c = self.read()\n        sign = 1\n        if c == ord('-'):\n            sign = -1\n            c = self.read()\n        val = 0\n        while c > 32:\n            val = val * 10 + (c - ord('0'))\n            c = self.read()\n        return val * sign\n\n    def nextIntArray(self, n):\n        arr = [0] * n\n        for i in range(n):\n            arr[i] = self.nextInt()\n        return arr\n\ndef main():\n    in_stream = Input(sys.stdin.buffer)\n    n = in_stream.nextInt()\n    b = in_stream.nextInt()\n    a = in_stream.nextIntArray(n)\n\n    odd = [0] * (n + 1)\n    even = [0] * (n + 1)\n\n    for i in range(1, n + 1):\n        odd[i] = odd[i - 1] + (a[i - 1] & 1)\n        even[i] = even[i - 1] + ((a[i - 1] ^ 1) & 1)\n\n    last = 0\n    costs = []\n    for i in range(1, n):\n        o = odd[i] - odd[last]\n        e = even[i] - even[last]\n        if o == e:\n            heapq.heappush(costs, abs(a[i] - a[i - 1]))\n            last = i\n\n    total = 0\n    count = 0\n    while costs and total <= b:\n        total += heapq.heappop(costs)\n        count += 1\n\n    if count == 0:\n        print(0)\n    else:\n        if not costs and total <= b:\n            print(count)\n        else:\n            print(count - 1)\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n0.95\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-5.447716102935374e-05, -1.6689286894688848e-06, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -1.0847986231965479e-05, -0.014138178899884224, -0.0002619877050165087, -0.0019306369358673692, -0.08957172185182571, -0.005296839866787195, -0.020543769001960754, -0.0001629458274692297, -4.887569048150908e-06, -7.152555099310121e-07, -3.576278118089249e-07, -3.6954811548639555e-06, -7.152555099310121e-07, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -1.0728830375228426e-06, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -5.602820692729438e-06, -4.9232225137529895e-05, -1.6689286894688848e-06, -4.887569048150908e-06, -0.0002475670480635017, -0.0332474522292614, 0.0, -1.6212332411669195e-05, -1.6927575416048057e-05, -5.960462772236497e-07, -9.536738616588991e-